"""Build the report from measured checks; pending evidence remains explicit."""
import pathlib,json,subprocess,sys
root=pathlib.Path('tmp/walkqa/harness-20')
subprocess.run([sys.executable,'tmp/walkqa/tools/results20.py'],check=True)
r=json.loads((root/'results.json').read_text());t=r['totals'];reviewed=sum(w.get('checks',{}).get('visual',{}).get('pass_') is not None for s in r['scenes'].values() for w in s['walks'].values())
keys=['lock','floor','scale','height','facing','draworder','path','clicks','exits','freeze','video','visual']
def values(s,key):
 ws=s['walks']
 if key in ('clicks','exits'):return [w.get('checks',{}).get('behavior',{}).get('pass_') for n,w in ws.items() if n.startswith('exit-')==(key=='exits')]
 return [w.get('checks',{}).get(key,{}).get('pass_') for w in ws.values()]
def status(v):
 if not v:return 'N/A'
 p=sum(x is True for x in v);f=sum(x is False for x in v);u=sum(x is None for x in v)
 return ('FAIL' if f else 'PENDING' if u else 'PASS')+f' {p}/{len(v)}'+(f' ({u} pending)' if u else '')
lines=['# Brief 20: ten-scene harness', '', '**FAIL — capture and visual review complete; repair loop incomplete. No Footfall sign-off.**', '',f'{t["capturedWalks"]}/{t["plannedWalks"]} planned walks captured across {t["scenes"]} scenes; {t["frames"]:,} logged frames. Full visual review recorded for {reviewed}/{t["plannedWalks"]} walks. **{t["passingWalks"]} walks pass all checks; {t["timedOutWalks"]} capture timed out and required a forced stop.** A failed capture, absent measurement, missing narration cache, or unreviewed sheet is never a pass.', '', 'All clips are local 1920×1080, 24 fps captures of the game; contact sheets sample 6 fps. No generative video was requested. Plans come from each live walk mask, extrema, clearance ridges and occluder baselines. Every scene remains in the run.', '', '## Scene × check', '', 'Cells show passing walks / applicable walks; one failing frame fails its walk. N/A means the scene supplied no exits.', '', '| Scene | Walks | '+' | '.join(keys)+' |', '|---|---|'+'---|'*len(keys)]
for name,s in r['scenes'].items():lines.append(f'| {name} | {s["captured"]}/{s["planned"]} | '+' | '.join(status(values(s,k)) for k in keys)+' |')
lines+=['','## Fixed defects','','- **Exit destination rebinding**, commit `7fe0a08`: narrative travel previously selected a generic far/left exit even when it was already bound elsewhere, causing HTTP 409. It now prefers the destination’s existing connection, otherwise an unbound exit. Three regression tests. Before/after narrative-run evidence: [before](../harness-20/narrative-before.json), [after](../harness-20/narrative-after.json). Subsequent missing-cache failures remain failures.','- **Unsafe support transfer after blocked settle**, commit `947e54a`: an unmatched standing recovery could transfer support to an airborne sole. It now keeps the safe support. Regression test reproduced the wrong R support before the fix and passes with L retained. Pier deepest changed from 13 incorrect-depth frames to zero; [before evidence](../harness-20/pier/attempt-1-before-recovery-fix/), [rerun](../harness-20/pier/deepest.mp4). This does not solve all blocked standing poses.','','## Retained limitations and open defects','','- **Alley crate, existing named limitation:** wall-backed crate has zero rear floor. Prior reviewer-approved evidence remains in [findings](findings.md) and `tmp/walkqa/verification-08/`. The alley has not been dropped or replaced.','- **Discrete stance steering and precise stopping:** two actual QA-browser repair trials are retained under [experiments](../harness-20/experiments/). Capping arrival tolerance at 12 px made outside near-left overrun into an exit (51.47% facing agreement); additionally constraining the cycle to the ground-space route heading still stopped 50.17 px short (82.09% agreement, below 95%). Baseline shortfall was 55.12 px and agreement 57.52%. Neither trial was installed. Church deepest trials are also retained.','- **Blocked rest poses:** church deepest frames 111–116 remain midstride after the support fix. Two steering/stop trials did not provide a satisfactory general solution. The guard fixes support safety, not the visual rest pose.','- **Narration fixture gaps:** all provider credentials remain disabled. Uncached corpus object options and some unconnected exits return 502. These behaviors fail; no fake narration or destination binding was inserted.','- **Lobby visual geometry:** feet show through stair risers and beneath the reception desk, despite some mask/baseline checks passing. See [narrow-gap crossing](../harness-20/lobby/narrow-gap-crops/crossing-review-000.png), [desk crossing](../harness-20/lobby/occluder-back-crops/crossing-review-000.png). This remains an open defect, not a waived pass.','','## Validation and operating constraints','','- Final source regression run: **435 tests / 47 files pass**, typecheck and lint pass. [Tests](../harness-20/tests-final.log), [typecheck](../harness-20/typecheck-final.log), [lint](../harness-20/lint-final.log).','- `verify:art`: all 16 stored scenes pass. [Log](../harness-20/art.log).','- Credential-disabled saved town replay after both fixes: **25 records, 28 cached calls, 0 uncached calls**. [Replay](../harness-20/town-replay.json), [log](../harness-20/town-final.log).','- Eight new metric checkers reject deliberately broken cases. [Self-tests](../harness-20/checker-selftests.log). Existing reviewer tools were not edited. `lockcheck.py` receives walk-log JSON files, never `area.json`.','- This brief has requested **0 segmentation calls, 0 image edits, 0 generative videos**. QA runs use API 4317/game 8080 with `?mute=1`; owner ports 4410/8090 remain untouched. No push, merge, deploy, key writes or dotenv edits. QA server cleanup is recorded in `harness-20/cleanup.json`.','','## Measurement scope','','Scale telemetry independently reconstructs the runtime perspective model at the nominal feet origin; planted-sole discrepancy is also reported. Pixel-height tracking uses actual video/background differences and compares against canonical source-cycle silhouette height. Censored/clipped measurements cannot establish a pass. Draw order uses sprite/occluder alpha intersection; the exterior includes Kat’s separate sprite, and all walks have zero bounding-box fallback frames. Path optimality uses an independent visibility graph on the raster-cell union; body clearance is an additional gate. The path gate includes both planned and actual body-origin distance ratios, plus body-clearance frames. Body-origin motion includes pose-origin offsets; this can overestimate physical travel. Pixel height uses one clean background per starting scene, so transitions and occlusion cannot establish a size pass. Facing uses a 30-degree angular tolerance and excludes launch/settle blends. These measurement limits do not waive visible defects.','','## Remaining work required by the brief', '', *['- '+x for x in r['openRequirements']], '', 'The 139 captured walks are not 139 successful coverage cases. A stationary click, a click intercepted by an object, or a gap candidate that is never traversed is a failed or unproven case. The narrow-gap generator finds a local clearance ridge; it does not prove this is the globally narrowest traversable passage. Nearest-reachable currently uses runtime preview rather than an independent projection. These are harness coverage gaps, not accepted scene limitations.', '', '## Walk evidence index','','Each link opens its 6 fps sheet; corresponding `.mp4`, `.json`, `-events.json`, `-check-*.json`, and `-crops/manifest.json` are beside it. Manifests record reviewed image hashes and visual observations.','','| Scene / walk | Frames | Failed checks | Pending checks | Visual observation |','|---|---:|---|---|---|']
for scene,s in r['scenes'].items():
 for name,w in s['walks'].items():
  c=w.get('checks',{});failed=[k for k,v in c.items() if v.get('pass_') is False];pending=[k for k,v in c.items() if v.get('pass_') is None]
  lines.append(f'| [{scene}/{name}](../harness-20/{scene}/{name}-sheet.png) | {w.get("frames","pending")} | {", ".join(failed) or "—"} | {", ".join(pending) or ("capture" if w["status"]=="pending" else "—")} | {w.get("visualNotes", "pending").replace(chr(124), "/")} |')
lines += ['', '## Defect register', '', pathlib.Path('tmp/walkqa/harness-20/defect-register.md').read_text()]
pathlib.Path('tmp/walkqa/reports/20-ten-scene-harness.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
print('Report refreshed:',reviewed,'visual reviews')
